# f1 = levelOf
# One of two twins (the other: ..as-an-integer.ir): `levelOf` is the same text in both and is handed to unseen code, so it reads by name, at a place. Beside it stand four classes that hold a field `level`, and their objects stay in sight, so the slots are narrow:
# three hold an object and one an integer, or one and three. The read calls the same stub in both. It went by the form that MOST layouts of the program hold the name in: two classes in another file changed which stub a function ran
